              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for to decide, then the Latin for to foresee."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: titulus, titulī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "titulus, titulī — \"a notice, a label; a title\". A shop or house could carry one by its door. The famous Pompeian doorway warning is a mosaic, but it reads like one: Cavē canem. — \"Beware of the dog.\" English title comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
